
# Switch on a platform with a switch of its own: NSSwitch on macOS, UISwitch on iOS, android.widget.Switch on
# Android, drawn and animated by the platform, with its accessibility and its feel (native-dom-0013). Reached through
# `component/switch.tree` by the `toolkit` rung of the macos, ios and android env chains.
#
# THE SAME CONTRACT as the generic ../switch.tree: `host`, `class`, and `control`, the disclosure controller (on =
# open). The author writes `view switch / bind control, read wifi` once and every platform honors it.
#
# `node switch` forces the element: inside a component named `switch`, `view switch` would be the component again.
# The toolkit host makes the platform's control for that tag, takes `aria-checked` as its state, and reports the
# platform's own change as `click`, which toggles the controller, whose effect writes the state back.

load @term/site/code/view/render
  find element
load @term/site/code/dom/dom
  find view
  find append
load ../../../logic/disclosure
  find disclosure-open
  find toggle-disclosure

task checked-text
  take control, like signal boolean
  like text
  save on
    call disclosure-open
      bind self, read control
  send back, text <{{on}}>

view switch
  take host, like view
  take class, like text
  take control, like signal boolean
  node switch
    bind data-slot, text <switch>
    bind aria-checked
      call checked-text
        read control
    bind class, read class
    hook click
      call toggle-disclosure
        bind self, read control
